# {name}

An OpenAI Agents SDK agent that remembers the people it talks to, with
[Alexein](https://alexein.ai). Made by `twinmemory-cli create openai-agents`.

## Run it

1. Fill in `.env`: `TWIN_MEMORY_API_KEY` (the console, under API keys) and `OPENAI_API_KEY`.
2. Talk to it in a terminal, as one of your users:

   ```bash
   uv run -m {package}.chat --user dana
   ```

3. `uvx twinmemory-cli doctor` checks the setup.

## What is where

- `src/{package}/agent.py` - the agent: memory is wired in here.
- `src/{package}/memory.py` - memory's recall, remember and tools, written by
  `twinmemory-cli init openai-agents`. Yours to edit.
- `src/{package}/chat.py` - the terminal chat.

Whose memory a run reads is the `user_id` in its context, set by your code and never by the model.
